Package: iscm
Type: Package
Title: The Inclusive Synthetic Control Method
Version: 0.1.2
Authors@R: c(
    person("Roberta", "Di Stefano", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "roberta.distefano@unimol.it"),
    person("Giovanni", "Mellace", role = c("aut"),
           email = "giome@sam.sdu.dk"))
Description: Implements the inclusive synthetic control method (iSCM) of
    Di Stefano and Mellace, a modification of synthetic control methods
    that allows units potentially affected by an intervention, directly or
    through spillovers, to remain in the donor pool. A synthetic control is
    constructed for the main treated unit and for every potentially affected
    unit, yielding a linear system that links the contaminated estimates to the
    effects of interest; solving the system removes the contamination exactly,
    without modifying the underlying estimator. The package provides the full and
    simplified iSCM, the restricted synthetic control benchmark, diagnostics for
    the conditioning of the correction, in-space placebo inference, and a
    pluggable estimator interface so that any SC-type backend can be used
    (dependency-free classic and penalized backends are included, with an
    optional wrapper around the 'Synth' package).
